# Deprecated APIs

- The guardrail check builds its list from `@deprecated` JSDoc on exported symbols in `packages/ai`, `packages/provider`, and `packages/provider-utils`, so the source is the truth, not this file.
- Common traps for engineers who learned an older SDK version: `generateObject` and `streamObject` (use `generateText` / `streamText` with an `output` setting), `ImagePart` (use `FilePart` with an image media type), `getToolOrDynamicToolName` (use `getToolName`).
- If you are unsure, open the declaration and read its `@deprecated` note.
